============================================================================================================
ARM 2 — FOLD ARITHMETIC (Sharpe of ANY stitched rule from precomputed sums)
============================================================================================================
  Sharpe(r) = sqrt(252) * mean/sd with sd on ddof=0, so a stitched series' Sharpe is a
  function of (n, sum r, sum r^2) accumulated over its folds only.  That makes a
  4,000-draw count-matched null exact and cheap; gated bit-for-bit below.
  [PASS] G3 sums-based Sharpe == direct Sharpe on stitched paths: 6.661e-16 (target < 1e-10)

============================================================================================================
ARM 3 — THE 36 REAL PUBLISH RULES, WALKED FORWARD
============================================================================================================
  At the start of fold Y a rule reads IS = [warm-up, Y-01-01) ONLY.  R_<L>@q moves to
  ladder L's IS-argmax rung when that rung's IS Sharpe exceeds the anchor's by more
  than q, else holds the anchor.  R_WIDEST@q does the same on whichever ladder has the
  widest IS Sharpe spread that fold.  R_ANCHOR never moves.  q is a REPORTED ladder,
  not a tuned dial: every value of q is published.

  41 rules per panel (5 ladder choices x 8 thresholds + R_ANCHOR).

